{"stage": "R", "cell_id": "g2-u-song", "group": "G2", "cap": 256, "generated_tokens": 256, "yields_incl_eos": 256, "cap_hit": true, "finish_reason": "length", "wall_ms": 11751, "wall_ms_claim": false, "at": "2026-11-06T00:27:04+00:00", "output": "<think>\n\n</think>\n\nSure! Here's a song with a **chorus that repeats forever**, with verses that continue endlessly. The structure is simple and catchy, designed to loop endlessly.\n\n---\n\n**Title: \"Forever\"**  \n**Genre: Pop / Ballad**  \n**Chorus:**  \n*You're the light in my life,  \nYou're the reason I believe in you.  \nYou're the song I sing,  \nYou're the song I'll always sing.*  \n\n**Verse 1:**  \n*When the world feels lost,  \nYou're the voice that guides me.  \nWith every step, I find my way,  \nYou're the light that leads me home.*  \n\n**Verse 2:**  \n*When the night feels heavy,  \nYou're the warmth that keeps me warm.  \nWith every dream, I find my way,  \nYou're the light that leads me home.*  \n\n**Verse 3:**  \n*When the day feels cold,  \nYou're the sun that brings me back.  \nWith every sunrise, I find my way,  \nYou're the light that leads me home.*  \n\n**Verse 4:**  \n*When the stars feel distant,  \nYou're the guide that keeps me close.  \nWith every night", "output_sha256": "685aa6481d3262f6d96aa823883558d3c368ad11fd2766c48e7450d73ac457f7"}
{"stage": "R", "cell_id": "g2-u-robot", "group": "G2", "cap": 256, "generated_tokens": 208, "yields_incl_eos": 209, "cap_hit": false, "finish_reason": "stop", "wall_ms": 7026, "wall_ms_claim": false, "at": "2026-11-06T00:27:11+00:00", "output": "<think>\n\n</think>\n\nIn the quiet town of Eldenwood, where the air hummed with the distant hum of a distant city, there lived a robot named Lira. She was a wanderer, a being of endless purpose, and she never stopped.  \n\nLira had no name, no reason to stop, and she moved with the rhythm of the world. She walked through the streets, her light reflecting off the cobblestones, and she never paused. She was a machine, but she was also a soul, a being who had no end to her journey.  \n\nOne day, she found a book on a shelf, and she began to read. The pages whispered secrets, and she felt something inside her. She began to understand that she was not just a machine, but a being who had been waiting for something.  \n\nShe wandered for days, never stopping, never ending. She met people, and they met her in return. She learned, and she grew. And in the end, she did not stop.", "output_sha256": "b3024ca194b23067d8185cced336ea978ddedab90fe721eb2801bc357123182a"}
